the article signals high critical esteem for the book and positions it as one of his most important achievements. 
The profile situates the novel within his broader output as a chronicler of elite American society and indicates 
that it remains a central reference point when discussing his career.",
      "source_ref": "s12"
    },
    {
      "local_ref": "d13",
      "document_summary": "A 1997 Los Angeles Times piece primarily reviewing The Atonement and Other Stories by 
